x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;peychaud&#39;s bitters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The world&#39;s second-most famous bitters is also the standard for the “New Orleans style” of aromatic cocktail finishers&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">peychaud&#39;s bitters</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/cherry-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJjaGVycnktaW5ncmVkaWVudC0yLnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJjaGVycnktaW5ncmVkaWVudC0yLnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJjaGVycnktaW5ncmVkaWVudC0yLnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;cherry&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;Arguably the most iconic cocktail garnish, this classic addition is usually not required, making it the ultimate exclamation point.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">cherry</a> or <a href="/ingredients/lemon-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lemon&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;One of the fundamental cocktail ingredients, lemon offers a clean, quick-hitting dose of brightness&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lemon peel</a> for garnish\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients in a mixing glass and stir</li>\n<li>Strain into a whiskey glass or cocktail glass, serve up with a garnish</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	4	[The Fine Art of Mixing Drinks](https://www.amazon.com/Fine-Art-Mixing-Drinks/dp/1603111646), David Embury, 1948	classic, stirred, up, cocktail glass, 			A simple Manhattan variation that subs Benedictine for vermouth
136	And To All A Goodnight	#Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1.5oz :[bourbon]\r\n* 0.75oz :[reposado tequila]\r\n* 0.75oz :[cherry heering]\r\n* 2dash :[orange bitters]\r\n* 1dash :[angostura bitters]\r\n* :[orange peel] for garnish\r\n\r\n#Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients in a mixing glass and stir over ice\r\n2. Strain into a cocktail glass and garnish	And to All a Goodnight is an audacious glass of holiday cheer created by Tim Stookey at the Presidio Social Club in San Francisco. It is an excellent execution of concept; a spirit forward holiday nightcap with all the winter warmth and spice to calm the restless anticipation of Santa’s arrival. This cranberry toned gem embraces an unusual combination of base spirits: tequila and :[bourbon]. Tequila is an adventurous change from the holiday norm, and the result is sure to be embraced by any =[Manhattan] lovers in your party.\r\n\r\nFor a drink with substantial :[cherry heering], this drink is very dry. The :[orange] bitters and aforementioned heering produce a fruit forward nose, and a sweetness that sits on the middle of the tongue. Tequila punctuates the finish and partners surprisingly well with bourbon for a whack of spice that compliments the large dosage of cherry nicely. It's a balancing act reminiscent of the =[Remember the Maine]. The :[orange] peel garnish is not simply for aesthetics; its oils soften the bitters and base spirits. To further balance the drink’s spiciness, use a sweeter bourbon. We do recommend sticking with bourbon, :[rye] will work, but requires additional heering. The recipe requests :[reposado tequila], but if you have anejo feel free to use it. This is the one time we request you be conservative with the bitters.\r\n	recipe-and-to-all-a-goodnight-cocktail-recipe.jpg	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	2016-12-24 23:50:36.817711	2021-04-10 20:30:20.509926	and-to-all-a-goodnight-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><sp