RpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;angostura bitters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The stalwart of the bitters category, this spicy bottle is used in an endless number of recipes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">angostura bitters</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/whisky-cocktail-recipes">bourbon</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/orange-liqueur-cocktail-recipes">orange liqueur</a> \n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine bitters, bourbon, and cointreau with ice and stir</li>\n<li>Strain into a chilled flute,  coupe, or cocktail glass</li>\n<li>Top with champagne</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, up, stirred, cocktail glass, 			A classic variation on the Champagne cocktail
73	Sleepy Resurrection	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1oz :[london dry gin]\r\n* 1oz :[rhubarb puree] (see below)\r\n* 0.5oz :[lemon juice] \r\n* 0.5oz :[benedictine]\r\n* 0.5oz :[lillet] \r\n* :[soda water] to fill\r\n* :[rosemary] sprig for garnish\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with ice and shake\r\n2. Strain into an cocktail glass\r\n3. Garnish with rosemary\r\n\r\n# Rhubarb Puree\r\n\r\n* 1lb rhubarb (about 4 stalks)\r\n* 0.5cup sugar\r\n* 0.25cup water\r\n* 0.25cup gin\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Chop rhubarb into quarter-inch pieces\r\n2. Simmer with water and sugar until soft\r\n3. Puree in a food processor \r\n4. Push through a fine mesh strainer or cheese cloth\r\n5. Combine with gin and refrigerate until needed 	Created for a friend’s annual spring party, the Sleepy Resurrection has its heart set on summer, but makes due with rainy days. :[Gin], :[Lillet], and :[Benedictine] all join forces for a sparkling slap of herbal goodness headlined by a goopy rhubarb puree. It’s a complex, tart, and easter-bunny pink adventure that screams “why doesn't April have any good drinking holidays?” The prep work is a bit annoying, but nobody said pastels were easy.\r\n\r\nTo make the rhubarb puree, cook down one pound of rhubarb with sugar and water, then process the mix and push it through a strainer. The finished product can vary a bit depending on the general mood of the rhubarb, particularly concerning tartness, so make sure to try your beverages before serving them. If they taste a bit flat, compensate with lemon. Occasionally, the finished product isn’t quite pink. If you are concerned your guests might feel suckered without an easter egg pallette, a quarter ounce of grenadine should fix things right up.\r\n\r\nThe flavor profile is all rosemary on first whiff, followed by tartness, then a big dose of herbaceousness from the Benedictine, Lillet, and rhubarb. It’s sweet but refreshing, and perfect for foggy spring days. We love Benedictine in this drink, especially since it doesn’t alter the rhubarb’s color, but [Chartreuse](http://www.tuxedono2.com/ingredients/green-chartreuse-cocktail-recipes) would work just fine in its place. The Lillet can be swapped for [Cocchi Americano](http://www.tuxedono2.com/ingredients/cocchi-americano-cocktail-recipes), or even dry vermouth. Just make sure to compensate a bit for the lost sweetness. Our favorite way to serve this drink is up with a big hunk of fresh rosemary, but we’ve also dispensed it over ice with a splash of soda and the results were just peachy.\r\n\r\n*Notice our pin? Great now fall victim to its sweet propaganda and go vote for us in the [Saveur Blog Awards](http://www.saveur.com/content/blog-awards-2015-vote?dom=spiritscocktail&src=2015blogbadge)!* 	recipe-sleepy-resurrection-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 12\n- 127\n- 17\n- 28\n- 15\n- 4\n- 126\n	t	2015-05-21 03:36:02.324919	\N	---\n- 1\n	2015-04-29 16:33:09.465843	2021-04-10 20:30:21.111598	sleepy-resurrection-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/gin-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ==&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjYwMCwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo2MDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;gin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;Unified by a liberal use of juniper, the gin family is one of the fundamental base spirits and a necessity in any bar&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">london dry gin</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/rhubarb-puree-cocktail-recipes">rhubarb puree</a> (see below)\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lemon-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lemon&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;One of the fundamental cocktail ingredients, lemon offers a clean, quick-hitting dose of brightness&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lemon juice</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/benedictine-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJiZW5lZGljdGluZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LTIucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJiZW5lZGljdGluZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LTIucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJiZW5lZGljdGluZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LTIucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;benedictine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The world&#39;s second-most-famous herbal liqueur is a little cheaper and a little more versatile than Chartreuse.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">benedictine</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lillet-cocktail-recipes">lillet</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/soda-water-cocktail-recipes">soda water</a> to fill\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/rosemary-cocktail-recipes">rosemary</a> sprig for garnish\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients with ice and shake</li>\n<li>Strain into an cocktail glass</li>\n<li>Garnish with rosemary</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h1>Rhubarb Puree</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>lb</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> rhubarb (about 4 stalks)\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>cup</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> sugar\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¼<span class='unit'>cup</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> water\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¼<span class='unit'>cup</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> gin\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Chop rhubarb into quarter-inch pieces</li>\n<li>Simmer with water and sugar until soft</li>\n<li>Puree in a food processor </li>\n<li>Push through a fine mesh strainer or cheese cloth</li>\n<li>Combine with gin and refrigerate until needed </li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		original, shaken, cocktail glass, up, 			A fun exploration in fresh spring flavors created for an Easter lunch
70	White Negroni	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1oz :[london dry gin] \r\n* 1oz :[lillet]  \r\n* 1oz :[salers] or :[suze]\r\n* :[lemon peel]  \r\n \r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with ice and stir\r\n2. Strain into a cocktail glass\r\n3. Garnish with lemon peel	The gentian genus makes up a small and herbaceous group of wild plants, known for their beautiful blue and yellow flowers. They are tough to farm, but flourish above the tree line in the alpine meadows of Europe, Turkey, and the Americas. The root is extremely bitter, and for centuries was taken as a digestive aid and cure-all. Today, it is used as a bittering agent in a plethora of iconic cocktail ingredients. :[Aperol], :[Campari], and :[Angostura bitters] all make use of it, but the best way to experience this grassy, mountain-meadowy goodness is in a gentian liqueur. These low alcohol aperitifs are light in color, making them perfect for mixed drinks. The tone does not adulterate a cocktail's color, and their earthy bitterness can add spice and surprise to an otherwise one dimensional drink. \r\n\r\nThe White Negroni is a fabulous use of the gentian's powers, and a downright brilliant twist on a bonafide classic. All of the flavor components of a classic =[Negroni] are present, but only the :[gin] remains verbatim. The bitter Campari is matched by the bitterness of the gentian liqueur, and the :[sweet vermouth] is replaced by an aperitif wine like :[Lillet]. Not only does this recipe go tit-for-tat with its ancestor, the ingredients are smartly chosen to be beautiful. Its milky white hue is a head-turning asset, and accordingly should never be shaken. For a spirit-forward variation, try dry vermouth instead of Lillet, or for something really special, take a crack at [The Great Outdoors](http://drinkstraightup.com/2013/05/27/the-great-outdoors/), one of our all-time favorites. No matter which you choose, take a moment to pour yourself a bit of that milky bitter stuff on the rocks. After all, how often does one get to drink the root-water of mountain flowers?\r\n	recipe-white-negroni-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 12\n- 15\n- 122\n- 124\n- 11\n	t	2015-03-18 20:17:10.711266	\N	---\n- 1\n	2015-03-18 20:03:08.773338	2021-04-10 20:30:21.129255	white-negroni-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/gin-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ==&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjYwMCwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo2MDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;gin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;Unified by a liberal use of juniper, the gin family is one of the fundamental base spirits and a necessity in any bar&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">london dry gin</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lillet-cocktail-recipes">lillet</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/salers-cocktail-recipes">salers</a> or <a href="/ingredients/suze-cocktail-recipes">suze</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/lemon-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lemon&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;One of the fundamental cocktail ingredients, lemon offers a clean, quick-hitting dose of brightness&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lemon peel</a><br>\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients with ice and stir</li>\n<li>Strain into a cocktail glass</li>\n<li>Garnish with lemon peel</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		stirred, up, cocktail glass, 			A great way to experience gentian liqueur in a tidy package
8	Test Pilot	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1.5oz :[dark rum]\r\n* 0.75oz :[light rum]\r\n* 0.5oz :[falernum]\r\n* 0.5oz :[orange liqueur]\r\n* 0.5oz :[lime juice]\r\n* 1dash :[angostura bitters]  \r\n* 1dash :[absinthe]  \r\n\r\n\r\n#Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with 1 cup crushed ice in a blender\r\n2. Blend for five seconds\r\n3. Pour, unstrained, over crushed ice	What makes a drink tough to prepare? Some cocktails are challenging _because_ they are simple, extracting complex flavors from a small troop of ingredients. Other drinks are tough because they require a battalion of bottles large enough to stock a small bar. If that second thing sounds good, then meet the Test Pilot: a triple axle of a cocktail. Each icy sip brims with molasses, clove, vanilla, and anise, spicy flavors perfect for cold weather or rainy days.  \r\n\r\nThe test pilot is complicated, but does not require finesse. So many voices are in this choir, a couple flat notes won’t be noticed. :[Light rum] and :[dark rum] are requested, but if this drink were prepared with only one #[rum], angels wouldn’t lose wings (though they might kindly recommend a second rum). For bigger bars, we prefer combining a smooth, team-playing label like Plantation 3-Star with something dark and buttery, such as Smith and Cross or Goslings. If this drink takes a nose dive, it will be with :[absinthe], so take it easy.   \r\n\r\nThe act of drink preparation—a serenade of aromas, colors, and history—has a zen appeal. For most, the clanky whir of a blender isn’t  part of that appeal. Releasing water into this drink is important, but a blender isn’t the only way. Paul Clarke of the [Cocktail Chronicles][1] recommends an immersion blender, a move we emphatically endorse. It’s quieter than a traditional blender, and offers a higher degree of control. If a mechanical chopping device isn’t in the house, pulverize some ice in a bag, and shake the thing to hell. This isn’t rocket science, and that’s alright. Rocket scientists need focus, and shouldn’t be drinking something this strong anyways.\r\n\r\n[1]: http://www.cocktailchronicles.com/\r\n	recipe-test-pilot-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 99\n- 26\n- 25\n- 13\n- 24\n- 20\n- 9\n	t	2015-02-12 04:43:57.425738	\N	---\n- 10\n- 1\n	2015-02-12 04:43:57.743847	2021-04-10 20:30:21.147892	test-pilot-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/rum-cocktail-recipes">dark rum</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¾<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/rum-cocktail-recipes">light rum</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/falernum-cocktail-recipes">falernum</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/orange-liqueur-cocktail-recipes">orange liqueur</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lime-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The preferred souring agent to many rum and gin drinks, lime is more mellow and complex than it&#39;s lemony cousin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lime juice</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>dash</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/angostura-bitters-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;angostura bitters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The stalwart of the bitters category, this spicy bottle is used in an endless number of recipes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">angostura bitters</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>dash</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/absinthe-cocktail-recipes">absinthe</a><br>\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients with 1 cup crushed ice in a blender</li>\n<li>Blend for five seconds</li>\n<li>Pour, unstrained, over crushed ice</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, crushed ice, tiki glass, shaken, 			A complex tiki drink that rewards with a blast confectionary flavors
56	Mai Tai	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1oz :[gold rum] \r\n* 1oz :[dark rum] \r\n* 1oz :[lime juice]\r\n* 0.5oz :[curacao]  or :[orange liqueur]\r\n* 0.25oz :[orgeat]\r\n* 0.25oz :[simple syrup] \r\n* :[mint] \r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with ice and shake \r\n2. Strain over crushed ice\r\n3. Submerge used lime shell and garnish with mint	The Mai Tai has a mixed up history. Reaching its height of popularity in the 50s and 60s, it is the quintessential tiki drink. Tiki trendsetters Don the Beachcomber and Trader Vic both claim to have invented the cocktail, though their versions are distinctly different. Over time all kinds of fruity concoctions have been whipped up under the name of Mai Tai, no doubt, in all the colors of the rainbow. Although itself slightly modified, due to availability of ingredients, Trader Vic’s ‘Original” Mai Tai reigns supreme.\r\n\r\nTiki drinks are often highly involved, requiring a laundry list of ingredients, some specifically crafted. In contrast, the Mai Tai is relatively simple. At the center of the drink is the french style almond syrup, :[orgeat]. If feeling ambitious, it is easily made at home, otherwise we recommend Small Hand Foods. Its hints of :[orange flower water] are accentuated by the :[Curacao]. Misinterpreted as fruit-centric, liquor actually accounts for a substantial portion of this cocktail, requiring a double dose of ice for suitable dilution. Make sure to pile the ice high, ideally snow cone style.\r\n\r\nThis is the time to have fun with garnishes. Perhaps set aside the plastic monkey, but loads of mint or creative cuts of fresh fruit compliment the tropical Tiki vibe. You might even be able to get away with a paper umbrella. We still suggest limiting it to one or two thoughtful items to avoid the fruit salad look of the drink's dark years. Now put on a surf album and enjoy.\r\n	recipe-mai-tai-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 98\n- 99\n- 24\n- 62\n- 13\n- 101\n- 7\n- 89\n	t	2015-04-02 02:55:00.412985	\N	---\n- 1\n- 60\n	2015-01-04 20:15:55.632684	2021-04-10 20:30:21.30894	mai-tai-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/rum-cocktail-recipes">gold rum</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/rum-cocktail-recipes">dark rum</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lime-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The preferred souring agent to many rum and gin drinks, lime is more mellow and complex than it&#39;s lemony cousin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lime juice</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/curacao-cocktail-recipes">curacao</a>  or <a href="/ingredients/orange-liqueur-cocktail-recipes">orange liqueur</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¼<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/orgeat-cocktail-recipes">orgeat</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¼<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/simple-flavored-syrup-cocktail-recipes">simple syrup</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/mint-cocktail-recipes">mint</a> \n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients with ice and shake </li>\n<li>Strain over crushed ice</li>\n<li>Submerge used lime shell and garnish with mint</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, shaken, crushed ice, rocks glass, 			A mid century tiki favorite that’s only slightly fruity
24	Corn N' Oil	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 2oz :[dark rum]\r\n* 0.5oz :[falernum]  \r\n* 0.3oz :[lime juice]  \r\n* 3dash :[angostura bitters]  \r\n* 1 :[lime wedge] for garnish\r\n\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients in a rocks glass\r\n2. Add crushed ice and stir\r\n3. Garnish with juiced lime shell	Often, those who love spirits love simple cocktails because they can tinker with them. A short recipe means fewer distractions and subsequently more breathing room for the complex ingredients they love. The :[whiskey] and :[gin] families are full of drinks like these, but #[rum] is a bit different. The members in this family are big and complicated, with recipes that look less like mixing instructions and more like fighter jet manuals. Fortunately, a handful of simple classics exist, allowing rum fans the freedom to enjoy their beloved spirit along with its many mixing companions.\r\n\r\nIn the ranks of great rum companions, :[falernum] is surely near the top. Many internet words have been spilled over this syrup and its foggy history, including a fable about how to say “you have to learn it” in a heavy Barbadian accent. The mixture itself infuses clove, lime, and almond into a base of sugar, water and rum. It has a low alcohol content and probably originated as a bottled form of a popular local punch. Most importantly: it’s inexpensive, generally well stocked, and fun and easy to make. We recommend making it, but the store bought stuff is good too. Hell, try both. Comparing them is fun and a bottle goes fast.\r\n\r\nThe Corn n' Oil is a simple drink that uses a lot of falernum, and the flavor profile follows suit. Each swig is chock full of clove, :[lime], vanilla, molasses and almond. It's a convincing rebuttal to those who think rum is only for summer. The classic recipe calls for [blackstrap rum](http://www.tuxedono2.com/ingredients/dark-rum-cocktail-recipes), but any dark and complex variety will do. We love to tinker, and seem to try a different variety every time, with few regrets. In fact, the only way to go wrong with this drink is to avoid it altogether.\r\n	recipe-corn-n-oil-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 99\n- 25\n- 24\n- 20\n- 54\n	t	2015-02-03 14:42:10.045061	\N	---\n- 1\n- 49\n	2015-01-30 00:01:00.450224	2021-04-10 20:30:21.158391	corn-n-oil-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>2<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/rum-cocktail-recipes">dark rum</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/falernum-cocktail-recipes">falernum</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>⅓<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lime-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The preferred souring agent to many rum and gin drinks, lime is more mellow and complex than it&#39;s lemony cousin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lime juice</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>3<span class='unit'>dash</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/angostura-bitters-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;angostura bitters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The stalwart of the bitters category, this spicy bottle is used in an endless number of recipes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">angostura bitters</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1</span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lime-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The preferred souring agent to many rum and gin drinks, lime is more mellow and complex than it&#39;s lemony cousin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lime wedge</a> for garnish\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients in a rocks glass</li>\n<li>Add crushed ice and stir</li>\n<li>Garnish with juiced lime shell</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, built in glass, crushed ice, rocks glass, fall, 			A dead easy path to rich island flavors
45	Penicillin	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 2oz blended :[scotch]  \r\n* 0.75oz :[lemon juice] \r\n* 0.75oz :[honey syrup]  \r\n* 3 slices fresh :[ginger]\r\n* 0.25oz islay single malt :[scotch]\r\n\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Muddle ginger in shaker\r\n2. Add blended Scotch, lemon, and syrup and shake with ice\r\n3. Strain into an ice filled old fashioned \r\n4. Float Islay Scotch on top\r\n\r\n	While this cocktail may not possess the groundbreaking healing properties of its namesake antibiotic, lets not dismiss the value of placebo effect. The Penicillin employs a cast of ingredients familiar to many home cure-alls, but drops the tea in favor of more :[Scotch]. The bold smoked flavors of this popular spirit can be intimidating, but with a resume that includes exceptional classics such as the =[Blood and Sand] and =[Rob Roy], it pays to be open minded.\r\n\r\nThe nose of this drink is full of smoky Scotch, followed by spicy :[ginger] on the tongue, and a sweet, mellow finish. The original recipe, created by bartender Sam Ross, calls for a ginger-honey syrup, but that has a short shelf life, and making a batch on demand might be excessive for the home bartender. To achieve a strong ginger flavor in fewer steps, make a :[honey syrup], then muddle slices of fresh ginger directly into the mix. This reduces the prep time, for easy construction whenever the mood strikes.\r\n\r\nBlended Scotch makes a good base, with rich layered flavors not unlike sweeter :[bourbon]. A smoky, strongly peated single malt such as an Islay whisky is harder to tame, but when used as a float, exudes campfire vibes perfect for melting away winter days. Pig's Nose blended Scotch is a staple of our bar, and a strong peated Scotch like Laphroaig will strike a good balance. \r\n\r\nHoney’s comforting richness is essential to balancing the Penicillin. In order to incorporate the naturally thick sweetener, thin it into a syrup. To prepare, simply warm equal parts honey and water and stir until combined. Unlike its ginger friend, this syrup will keep. Put it to use in future rounds, or mix it into a =[Spruce Goose].	recipe-penicillin-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 55\n- 17\n- 56\n- 83\n- 84\n	t	2015-01-22 20:57:29.903496	\N	---\n- 1\n	2015-01-22 06:24:46.19029	2021-04-10 20:30:21.177508	penicillin-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>2<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> blended <a href="/ingredients/whisky-cocktail-recipes">scotch</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¾<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lemon-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lemon&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;One of the fundamental cocktail ingredients, lemon offers a clean, quick-hitting dose of brightness&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lemon juice</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¾<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/simple-flavored-syrup-cocktail-recipes">honey syrup</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>3</span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> slices fresh <a href="/ingredients/ginger-cocktail-recipes">ginger</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¼<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> islay single malt <a href="/ingredients/whisky-cocktail-recipes">scotch</a>\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Muddle ginger in shaker</li>\n<li>Add blended Scotch, lemon, and syrup and shake with ice</li>\n<li>Strain into an ice filled old fashioned </li>\n<li>Float Islay Scotch on top</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	4		shaken, large cube, rocks glass, winter, 			Smoke and ginger combine for a breathtaking modern classic
58	Spruce Goose	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 2oz :[new american gin] \r\n* 0.5oz :[honey syrup] \r\n* 0.5oz :[lime juice] \r\n* 0.25oz :[angostura bitters] \r\n* sprinkle of :[salt]\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with ice and shake\r\n2. Strain into a coupe and sprinkle with salt	First spotted on the menu at [Alameda][1], one of our favorite Brooklyn cocktail establishments, the Spruce Goose didn’t seem like much. Printed as a mixture of gin, lime, and Angostura, it wasn’t exactly jumping off the page, and contributed to a cocktail indifference that lasted several visits. It took an extended stay, encompassing several rounds, to finally surface this drink. Of course, after the first one, we were hooked. \r\n\r\nThe Spruce Goose is a simple twist on a very old cocktail: the =[Alabazam]. Like its older sibling, the Goose is transformed by copious amounts of bitters. Unlike the Alabazam, it calls for a base spirit of gin, a risky move that pays off in spades. The fragrant bouquet of good gin melds into Angostura’s spicy clove for a scent that pursues divinity. The sip strikes a unique balance between spicy and refreshing. It’s an exceptional twist on an old drink with some outside-the-box flavor pairing.\r\n\r\nBest of all, the drink is not hard to make. Alameda makes their Spruce Goose with [St. George’s Terroir Gin][2], a move we emphatically endorse, but any decent stuff will do. If an American gin is in the house, spring for that. Last we checked, Alameda is serving their Gooses over ice. This is a fine way to drink them, but we prefer the big nose and silky texture obtained when the drink is served up.\r\n\r\n[1]: http://alamedanyc.com/\r\n[2]: http://www.stgeorgespirits.com/spirits/gins/st-george-terroir-gin/	recipe-spruce-goose-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 12\n- 56\n- 24\n- 20\n- 104\n	t	2015-01-04 20:30:56.10432	\N	---\n- 1\n	2015-01-04 20:30:56.223905	2021-04-10 20:30:21.187565	spruce-goose-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>2<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/gin-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ==&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjYwMCwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo2MDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;gin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;Unified by a liberal use of juniper, the gin family is one of the fundamental base spirits and a necessity in any bar&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">new american gin</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/simple-flavored-syrup-cocktail-recipes">honey syrup</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lime-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The preferred souring agent to many rum and gin drinks, lime is more mellow and complex than it&#39;s lemony cousin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lime juice</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¼<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/angostura-bitters-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;angostura bitters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The stalwart of the bitters category, this spicy bottle is used in an endless number of recipes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">angostura bitters</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'>sprinkle of <a href="/ingredients/salt-cocktail-recipes">salt</a>\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients with ice and shake</li>\n<li>Strain into a coupe and sprinkle with salt</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		shaken, up, cocktail glass, 			A riff on the Alabazam, complete with boatloads of bitters
60	Champagne Cocktail	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* :[champagne]\r\n* 1 :[sugar cube] \r\n* 3dash :[angostura bitters] \r\n* splash of :[brandy] , optional\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Place sugar cube in glass and top with bitters\r\n2. If using, add brandy\r\n3. Gently pour in Champagne	The Champagne Cocktail is a timeless showstopper. :[Champagne] itself is an indulgence for many, but there are celebrations that demand gilding the lily. This cocktail is the only bit of opulence fit to accompany the aggressively indulgent dropping of multiple tons of Waterford Crystal over a crowd of Yankee dandies. So ring in the New Year with a drink of equal parts science experiment and sequined dress. \r\n\r\nThe classic Champagne Cocktail is a simple mixture: soak a :[sugar cube] in bitters and top with Champagne. When selecting a bubbly, there are two camps. The drink’s reliance on sparkling wine suggests a top shelf option is best suited to the role, however the purist would not dare pollute the natural delights of authentic Champagne. We favor economy, and suggest a tasty dry prosecco or cava. The drier the better to avoid sugar overload. If feeling particularly fancy, add a splash of quality :[brandy]; the spirit partners with bitters to warm the drink’s crisp sweetness. The classic recipe employs :[Angostura bitters], but there's plenty of room for creativity. To dress this drink to the nines we recommend Bittermens Burlesque Bitters. The slightly exotic hibiscus blend is ideal for a truly swanky soiree.\r\n\r\nFor optimal drama prepare the sugar cube in a glass and pour in the bubbly at the last minute. The cocktail’s glamour surfaces as the sugar cube dissolves in Champagne. As cute as a vintage coupe may seem, to maximize the effect and retain effervescence make sure to use a Champagne flute. 	recipe-champagne-cocktail-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 18\n- 8\n- 20\n- 48\n	t	2015-01-04 20:30:38.879213	\N	---\n- 1\n	2015-01-04 20:30:39.012733	2021-04-10 20:30:21.208414	champagne-cocktail-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/champagne-cocktail-recipes">champagne</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1</span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/sugar-cube-cocktail-recipes">sugar cube</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>3<span class='unit'>dash</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/angostura-bitters-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhbmdvc3R1cmEtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;angostura bitters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The stalwart of the bitters category, this spicy bottle is used in an endless number of recipes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">angostura bitters</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'>splash of <a href="/ingredients/brandy-cocktail-recipes">brandy</a> , optional\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Place sugar cube in glass and top with bitters</li>\n<li>If using, add brandy</li>\n<li>Gently pour in Champagne</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, built in glass, up, 			One of the all-time classics, this drink goes big on flavor and easy on the booze
120	Gimlet	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 2oz :[london dry gin]\r\n* 0.75oz :[lime cordial]\r\n* 0.75oz fresh :[lime juice]\r\n* :[lime peel] for garnish\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients in a shaker and shake\r\n2. Strain into a chilled coupe and garnish\r\n\r\n# Lime Cordial\r\n\r\n* 1cup sugar\r\n* 1cup water\r\n* 4 limes\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Zest limes with microplane or grater\r\n2. In a pot, combine water and sugar, stir until completely dissolved\r\n3. Add lime zest and let infuse for 10 minutes. Bottle and refrigerate.\r\n\r\n_(adapted from [PDT](https://www.amazon.com/PDT-Cocktail-Book-Bartenders-Celebrated/dp/1402779232))_	In the 1800s, scurvy tormented those who worked the high seas. It was known that citrus helped ward off this nutritional menace, but fresh fruit was susceptible to spoil and vermin. To combat this, juices were preserved in alcohol, but this had problems too: some workers didn’t drink, and those who did found the mixture unpalatable. Lauchlin Rose, who founded Rose’s in 1867, patented a method to preserve lime juice with sugar instead of alcohol. Because of its broad appeal, :[lime cordial] became wildly popular with shipping companies and naval establishments. \r\n\r\nAs the story goes, the term *Gimlet* derives from the surname of British Surgeon General Sir Thomas Gimelette, who instituted a daily ration of lime cordial for active Navy members. Some stories claim Gimelette ordered the cordial be mixed directly into each tot of :[gin], but this seems unlikely. Forcing the cordial to be mixed with alcohol would negate one of its chief benefits: teetotaler friendliness. A more likely story is that Gimelette preferred to take *his* lime cordial with a bit of gin, which undoubtedly also proved popular with sailors trying to force down government liquor.\r\n\r\nLight, refreshing, and almost dangerously drinkable, the Gimlet is perfect for daytime events and easy-peasy celebrations. The simplicity of the recipe also makes it a great cocktail to tinker with, and a simple way to try out a new and exciting gin. It has a soft green hue with a milky, opaque consistency. It's a bit sweeter than a =[daiquiri], and has a double dose of lime from the infused syrup. The nose sparkles with juniper and fruit, and the sip opens with sourness, followed by smooth sweetness.\r\n\r\nThe original gimlet contained only lime cordial and gin, but today many recipes call for the combination of fresh :[lime] and simple syrup instead. Excluding those seeking a sip of history, the version with fresh lime juice will taste better. The one downside to this variation is the absence of infused lime peel, which tastes distinctly different from juice, and is present in most lime cordials. Our favorite solution to this problem is from the [PDT Cocktail Book][1]: they use a quick and easy syrup infusion. We've taken that recipe, reprinted it here, and converted it to a size better for small bars. If you don't feel like making the infused syrup, don't let that keep you from making the drink; use plain 1:1 simple syrup instead. Many books recommend Plymouth gin in this recipe, but don’t hesitate to branch out. This simple old bird is fabulously open-minded.\r\n\r\n[1]: https://www.amazon.com/PDT-Cocktail-Book-Bartenders-Celebrated/dp/1402779232	recipe-gimlet-cocktail-recipe.jpg	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	2016-09-26 14:57:36.306424	2021-04-10 20:30:20.631112	gimlet-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>2<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/gin-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ==&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJnaW4taW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjYwMCwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo2MDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;gin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;Unified by a liberal use of juniper, the gin family is one of the fundamental base spirits and a necessity in any bar&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">london dry gin</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¾<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lime-cordial-cocktail-recipes">lime cordial</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¾<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> fresh <a href="/ingredients/lime-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The preferred souring agent to many rum and gin drinks, lime is more mellow and complex than it&#39;s lemony cousin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lime juice</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/lime-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsaW1lLWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lime&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The preferred souring agent to many rum and gin drinks, lime is more mellow and complex than it&#39;s lemony cousin&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lime peel</a> for garnish\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients in a shaker and shake</li>\n<li>Strain into a chilled coupe and garnish</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h1>Lime Cordial</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>cup</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> sugar\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>cup</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> water\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>4</span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> limes\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Zest limes with microplane or grater</li>\n<li>In a pot, combine water and sugar, stir until completely dissolved</li>\n<li>Add lime zest and let infuse for 10 minutes. Bottle and refrigerate.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p><em>(adapted from <a href="https://www.amazon.com/PDT-Cocktail-Book-Bartenders-Celebrated/dp/1402779232">PDT</a>)</em></p>\n	\N	f	0		classic, shaken, up, cocktail glass, 			Dead easy lime and gin with naval origins
40	Stardust	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1.5oz :[reposado tequila] \r\n* 1oz :[creme de cacao]  \r\n* 1oz :[heavy cream]  \r\n* 0.5oz :[cinnamon syrup]  \r\n* splash of :[absinthe]  \r\n* whole :[star anise] for garnish\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Coat glass with absinthe\r\n2. Combine remaining ingredients with ice and shake\r\n3. Strain and garnish with star anise\r\n\r\n# Cinnamon Syrup\r\n\r\n* 1cup sugar\r\n* 1cup water\r\n* 4 :[cinnamon] sticks\r\n\r\n# Instructions \r\n\r\n1. Heat all ingredients until sugar has dissolved\r\n2. Let cool and remove cinnamon sticks	To up your holiday cheer game, we gift you one of our favorite house recipes: The Stardust. We conjured up this drink to share with friends at our legendary Christmas parties. Holiday menus tend to overemphasize dark spirits; to balance ours and add a bit of variety, we turned to #[tequila]. This choice is rarely sipped while decking the halls (at least in the midwest North American traditions we’re accustomed to), but tequila’s natural sweetness and warmth play nicely with classic seasonal fixings. :[Absinthe] and :[heavy cream] are old friends, rarely found mingling with tequila, but here they make a delightful eggnog alternative. We weren’t without help: both the [North Star][1] by Post Prohibition and the classic Alexander cocktail provided inspiration. \r\n\r\nWhiffs of anise transition to the soft wintery comforts of vanilla, cocoa, and :[cinnamon]. Chocolate and tequila are natural partners, marrying earthy with sweet. Tequila intervenes, preventing this cocktail from approaching confection. The absinthe is mellowed by the luxurious texture of cream, an indulgence perfect for the holidays. For those who don’t drink dairy, coconut milk is a fine alternative, but we recommend increasing its measure to 1.5 ounces. This alternative is a bit sharper on the tongue, but still festive and rich.  [As always][2], choose wisely with :[creme de cacao]. We recommend Tempus Fugit for something natural but not too sweet.\r\n\r\n[1]: http://postprohibition.com/recipes/the-north-star/\r\n[2]: http://tuxedono2.com/20th-century-cocktail-recipe	recipe-stardust-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 42\n- 40\n- 32\n- 73\n- 9\n- 76\n- 90\n	t	2015-04-02 02:22:31.63126	\N	---\n- 1\n- 8\n- 54\n	2015-01-04 20:16:01.632684	2021-04-10 20:30:21.217684	stardust-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/tequila-cocktail-recipes-2b696998-9451-4199-b57f-4ff9f2a881b1" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhZ2F2ZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhZ2F2ZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhZ2F2ZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;tequila&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;A newer member of the cocktail base spirit club, tequila shines in almost any moment— but most when the days are long&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">reposado tequila</a> \n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/creme-de-cacao-cocktail-recipes">creme de cacao</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/heavy-cream-cocktail-recipes">heavy cream</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/simple-flavored-syrup-cocktail-recipes">cinnamon syrup</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'>splash of <a href="/ingredients/absinthe-cocktail-recipes">absinthe</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'>whole <a href="/ingredients/star-anise-cocktail-recipes">star anise</a> for garnish\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Coat glass with absinthe</li>\n<li>Combine remaining ingredients with ice and shake</li>\n<li>Strain and garnish with star anise</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h1>Cinnamon Syrup</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>cup</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> sugar\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>cup</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> water\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>4</span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/cinnamon-cocktail-recipes">cinnamon</a> sticks\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Heat all ingredients until sugar has dissolved</li>\n<li>Let cool and remove cinnamon sticks</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		original, shaken, cocktail glass, up, 			An offbeat tequila combination with holiday gusto
21	Sidecar	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1.5oz :[brandy]\r\n* 0.75oz :[orange liqueur]\r\n* 0.75oz :[lemon juice]\r\n* :[sugar] for rim\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. If to your taste, sugar the rim of a coupe\r\n2. Combine all ingredients with ice and shake\r\n3. Strain into glass, serve up\r\n\r\n	Before the sidecar adorned cocktail menus, it upgraded the daily commute. In the teens and twenties, passenger vehicles were very expensive, making motorcycles a popular alternative in Europe’s small cities. The cocktail, invented around the same time, probably got its name from an uninspired glance across the street. So much for creativity. \r\n\r\nBlame it on the name, the origin story, or perhaps the :[brandy], but something is distinctly European about the Sidecar. It has been described as a "brandy daiquiri", which is both accurate and also unfair to a drink with a distinguished, century-long reputation. Like the =[daiquiri], the Sidecar is a balancing act of sweet and sour, with the ultimate goal of underlining its fabulous spirit. Unlike its Cuban brethren, the sidecar is nuttier, fruitier, and full-bodied. \r\n\r\nTwo of the three ingredients in this drink are very unpredictable. :[Lemon]s range from sour to sweet depending on the crop, while brandy is, well, brandy. When mixing, pour a taste into a shot glass. If time permits, do the sugar rim. It looks good and usually earns a bonus point for unexpectedness.\r\n	recipe-sidecar-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 48\n- 13\n- 17\n	t	2014-12-11 05:34:52.511957	\N	---\n- 1\n- 56\n- 59\n- 38\n	2015-01-04 20:15:57.632684	2021-04-10 20:30:21.28249	sidecar-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/brandy-cocktail-recipes">brandy</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¾<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/orange-liqueur-cocktail-recipes">orange liqueur</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>¾<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/lemon-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJsZW1vbi1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;lemon&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;One of the fundamental cocktail ingredients, lemon offers a clean, quick-hitting dose of brightness&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">lemon juice</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/sugar-cocktail-recipes">sugar</a> for rim\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>If to your taste, sugar the rim of a coupe</li>\n<li>Combine all ingredients with ice and shake</li>\n<li>Strain into glass, serve up</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, shaken, up, cocktail glass, 			One of the all-time classic sours, distinguished by a sugar rim
23	Oaxaca Old Fashioned	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1.5oz :[reposado tequila]  \r\n* 0.5oz :[mezcal]\r\n* 1tsp :[agave syrup]\r\n* 2dash :[mole bitters] or :[chocolate bitters]\r\n* :[orange peel] for garnish \r\n\r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with ice and stir\r\n2. Strain into an old fashioned over ice \r\n3. Flame orange peel and garnish	The Oaxaca Old Fashioned could also be called a Mezcal Old Fashioned, but that seems like poor advertising for a drink that is very different. Toying with bitters, or the way sugar is added, are both acceptable ways of tinkering with the :[bourbon] based classic. Swapping out whiskey and dumping in :[mezcal]? That sounds downright blasphemous. \r\n\r\nThe Oaxaca Old Fashioned is not blasphemous, because it is no more a “Mezcal Old Fashioned” than a =[Sidecar] is a “Cognac Daiquiri.” The recipe is different in so many ways, it is unproductive to bother comparing them. That’s fine with us, because this recipe is so exceptional, it could be a classic on its own. It's brilliantly balanced, the agave spirits producing a surprisingly smooth union of smoky and sweet. A finish of chocolate warmth from the :[mole bitters] highlights the blend’s earthy notes. It’s a superb pairing, but as a backup :[angostura bitters] make a fine alternative. This is for timid mezcal drinkers, a great way to introduce them to the spirit. For those who want more smoke, bump up the measure of mezcal. One could even omit the tequila, but that might be taking it too far.\r\n\r\nThe flamed :[orange] peel is a delightful finish, its sweetness complimenting the :[reposado tequila], and the touch of fire complimenting the smoky mezcal. For more detailed instructions on how to flame an orange, see our recipe for the =[Blood and Sand]. That said, don’t let a lack of garnish halt the mixing of this drink. With or without the peel, it will impress.\r\n	recipe-oaxacan-old-fashioned-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 42\n- 50\n- 51\n- 52\n- 77\n- 49\n	t	2014-12-10 18:50:52.580059	\N	---\n- 1\n- 54\n- 58\n	2015-01-04 20:15:59.632684	2021-04-10 20:30:21.247822	oaxacan-old-fashioned-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/tequila-cocktail-recipes-2b696998-9451-4199-b57f-4ff9f2a881b1" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhZ2F2ZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhZ2F2ZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhZ2F2ZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;tequila&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;A newer member of the cocktail base spirit club, tequila shines in almost any moment— but most when the days are long&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">reposado tequila</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/tequila-cocktail-recipes-2b696998-9451-4199-b57f-4ff9f2a881b1" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJhZ2F2ZS1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLC