OnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;benedictine&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The world&#39;s second-most-famous herbal liqueur is a little cheaper and a little more versatile than Chartreuse.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">benedictine</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>3<span class='unit'>dash</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/orange-bitters-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJvcmFuZ2UtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJvcmFuZ2UtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6MzAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjMwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJvcmFuZ2UtYml0dGVycy1pbmdyZWRpZW50LnBuZyIsImVkaXRzIjp7InJlc2l6ZSI6eyJ3aWR0aCI6NjAwLCJoZWlnaHQiOjYwMCwiZml0IjoiY292ZXIifX19 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;orange bitters&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The perfect compliment to gin, these fruity bitters are easily employed in a great many drinks&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">orange bitters</a>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'></span><span class='ingredient'><a href="/ingredients/orange-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJvcmFuZ2UtaW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ==&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJvcmFuZ2UtaW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjMwMCwiaGVpZ2h0IjozMDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJvcmFuZ2UtaW5ncmVkaWVudC5wbmciLCJlZGl0cyI6eyJyZXNpemUiOnsid2lkdGgiOjYwMCwiaGVpZ2h0Ijo2MDAsImZpdCI6ImNvdmVyIn19fQ== 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;orange&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The mellowest of all the cocktail citrus, orange perks up everything from tiki drinks to old classics&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">orange peel</a> for garnish\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients over ice in a mixing glass and stir, about 10-15 seconds</li>\n<li>Strain into a cocktail glass and garnish</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, stirred, up, cocktail glass, fall, 			A complex and herbal Benedictine laced spin on the martini
7	Alabazam	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 2oz :[cognac]\r\n* 0.5oz :[orange liqueur]\r\n* 0.5oz :[lemon juice]  \r\n* 0.25oz :[simple syrup]  \r\n* 0.25oz :[angostura bitters]  \r\n\r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with ice and shake\r\n2. Strain into a chilled cocktail glass, serve up	Looking for a way to burn through that bottle of [Angostura bitters](http://www.tuxedono2.com/ingredients/angostura-bitters-cocktail-recipes) purchased for an [Old Fashioned](http://www.tuxedono2.com/old-fashioned-cocktail-recipe)? Well, you’re welcome. The Alabazam is a truly old school cocktail from the days when bitters concoctions served as medicinal tonics. Expat Leo Engel takes credit for the drink, dated 1878, well before bitters were relegated to increasingly subservient roles. Accustomed to drinks with one or two dashes, this unusual dose now seems fresh and innovative. We’re drinking backwards, enlivening our palates with a spicy complexity that has been snubbed for too long.\r\n\r\nThe Alabazam bears resemblance to a [Sidecar](http://www.tuxedono2.com/sidecar-cocktail-recipe), but the large dosage of Angostura completely alters the profile. The color changes dramatically, shifting from pale orange to a deep, juicy red. Despite fears of a bitter domination, everything meshes swimmingly. At the nose, it's all spice and citrus. Bitters and [cognac](http://www.tuxedono2.com/ingredients/cognac-cocktail-recipes) combine for an earthy balance, spicing up the spirit’s fruitiness and smoothing any bitter tones. For the base, grab a good cognac such as Pierre Ferrand. If no [Cointreau](http://www.tuxedono2.com/ingredients/cointreau-cocktail-recipes) is on hand, [Curacao](http://www.tuxedono2.com/ingredients/curacao-cocktail-recipes) is a fine alternative. Shaking all of this Angostura creates a creamy and surprisingly luxurious texture.	recipe-alabazam-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 21\n- 13\n- 17\n- 7\n- 20\n	t	2015-01-15 04:52:58.281976	\N	---\n- 1\n- 56\n- 59\n- 17\n- 38\n	2015-