div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;cherry&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;Arguably the most iconic cocktail garnish, this classic addition is usually not required, making it the ultimate exclamation point.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">cherry</a>  for garnish\n</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h1>Instructions</h1>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all ingredients with ice and stir</li>\n<li>Strain into a cocktail glass</li>\n<li>Garnish with a cherry</li>\n</ol>\n	\N	f	0		classic, stirred, up, cocktail glass, 			The godfather of whisky cocktails
36	Boulevardier	# Recipe\r\n\r\n* 1.5oz :[bourbon]  \r\n* 1oz :[campari]   \r\n* 1oz :[sweet vermouth]  \r\n* :[orange peel], :[lemon peel], or :[cherry], for garnish\r\n \r\n# Instructions\r\n\r\n1. Combine all ingredients with ice and stir vigorously \r\n2. Strain into a coupe, serve up\r\n	The Boulevardier is a prohibition era cocktail created to satisfy the tastes of Americans in Paris. Teetotalism sent many across the pond, introducing continental ingredients to American mixologists. This recipe could be an Americanized [Negroni](http://tuxedono2.com/negroni-cocktail-recipe) or a Europeanized [Manhattan](http://tuxedono2.com/manhattan-cocktail-recipe), depending on interpretation. The Boulevardier relies on the common trio of liquor, bitter, and vermouth. It combines these ingredients with equal success, but doesn’t seem to get the same love as its siblings. This is a shame, as it offers the best of two worlds, and is sure to please fans of each.\r\n\r\nThe Boulevardier enlivens American [bourbon](http://tuxedono2.com/ingredients/bourbon-cocktail-recipes) with the distinctly European [Campari](http://tuxedono2.com/boulevardier-cocktail-recipe). Like its Italian relative, this was originally an equal parts cocktail. It has become common practice to bump up the whiskey, better balancing the intensity of its bitter companion. A spicy, high proof bourbon would probably be robust enough to work with the original ratio. Regardless, the base spirit imparts a richness that amplifies the bittersweet balance of Campari and [Vermouth](http://tuxedono2.com/ingredients/sweet-vermouth-cocktail-recipes), resulting in a smooth autumnal alternative to the Negroni, or a Manhattan with an earthier complexity.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe garnish is a matter of preference. A [lemon peel](http://tuxedono2.com/ingredients/lemon-peel-cocktail-recipes) adds a clean hint of acidity, and is a nice color contrast in a sea of red. An [orange](http://tuxedono2.com/list/orange-cocktail-recipes) wedge fits the Negroni angle, and looks pretty balancing on the edge of a coupe. For a sweeter choice, the Manhattan fan will feel most at home with a [cherry](http://tuxedono2.com/ingredients/cherry-cocktail-recipes).	recipe-boulevardier-cocktail-recipe.jpg	---\n- 19\n- 1\n- 2\n	t	2014-12-10 19:13:31.579109	\N	---\n- 49\n- 1\n	2015-01-04 20:15:43.632684	2022-06-13 04:29:40.594795	boulevardier-cocktail-recipe	<h1>Recipe</h1>\n\n<ul>\n<li><span class='amount'>1½<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/whisky-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--subcomponent&#39;&gt;&lt;img class=&#39;tooltip__image&#39; src=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJ3aGlza2V5LWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0=&#39; srcset=&#39;https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJ3aGlza2V5LWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjozMDAsImhlaWdodCI6MzAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 1x, https://d34nm4jmyicdxh.cloudfront.net/eyJidWNrZXQiOiJjaHJpc3N5LXR1eGVkby1ubzIiLCJrZXkiOiJ3aGlza2V5LWluZ3JlZGllbnQucG5nIiwiZWRpdHMiOnsicmVzaXplIjp7IndpZHRoIjo2MDAsImhlaWdodCI6NjAwLCJmaXQiOiJjb3ZlciJ9fX0= 2x&#39;/&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__title&#39;&gt;whiskey&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip__description&#39;&gt;The basis for many all-time classics, the history of the cocktail is inextricably intertwined with this humble grain spirit &lt;/div&gt;&lt;svg class=&#39;tooltip__tip&#39;&gt;&lt;use href=&#39;/dist/sprite.svg#tooltip-tip-white&#39;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">bourbon</a><br>\n</span></li>\n<li><span class='amount'>1<span class='unit'>oz</span></span><span class='divider'></span><span class='ingredient'> <a href="/ingredients/campari-cocktail-recipes" tooltip="&lt;div class=&#39;tooltip tooltip--component&#39;&gt;&lt;img c